@lang en
IMPORT `homecare-part3`

-- Tests for Part 3 (additional benefits) and the General Conditions, with traces of the
-- duties. Expected values were worked from the source text (clauses cited) before the
-- assertions were run. Summary figures are the HYPOTHETICAL ones of homecare-test-fixtures.l4:
-- the owner's Part 1 sums insured total 2,500,000,000, so the 10% accommodation limit is
-- 250,000,000; no Part 3 Deductible.

§ `Tests: Part 3 and the General Conditions`

§§ `Part 3: temporary accommodation and rent (src:630-654)`

GIVEN damage   IS A `A Part 1 loss`
      unfit    IS A BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A `A capacity`
      months   IS A NUMBER
      `rent`   IS A NUMBER
      `extra`  IS A NUMBER
      `paid`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A temporary accommodation claim`
`an accommodation claim: damage` damage `, unfit` unfit `, as` capacity `, months` months `, rent lost` `rent` `, extra cost` `extra` `, paid earlier` `paid` MEANS
    `A temporary accommodation claim` WITH
        `the damage to the Home`                        IS damage
        `the Home is unfit for occupation`              IS unfit
        `the capacity`                                  IS capacity
        `months needed to restore or repair the Home`   IS months
        `rent lost`                                     IS `rent`
        `additional cost of temporary accommodation`    IS `extra`
        `paid under this benefit earlier in the Period` IS `paid`

GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
      `extra` IS A NUMBER
      `paid`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the owner-occupier is paid, for months` months `, extra cost` `extra` `, paid earlier` `paid` MEANS
    `Part 3: the accommodation or rent payable, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct`
        `for` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `owner-occupier` `, months` months `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` `extra` `, paid earlier` `paid`)
        `, as at` `1 April 2026`

-- 3 months of 6: half the 250,000,000 limit, 125,000,000; an extra cost of 80,000,000 is paid
-- in full, one of 150,000,000 is cut to 125,000,000.
#ASSERT `the owner-occupier is paid, for months` 3 `, extra cost` 80_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0 EQUALS 80_000_000
#ASSERT `the owner-occupier is paid, for months` 3 `, extra cost` 150_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0 EQUALS 125_000_000
-- 9 months needed: the 6 insured months bound it, so the whole 250,000,000 is available.
#ASSERT `the owner-occupier is paid, for months` 9 `, extra cost` 300_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0 EQUALS 250_000_000
-- 200,000,000 paid earlier in the Period leaves 50,000,000 (F-p3-shared).
#ASSERT `the owner-occupier is paid, for months` 6 `, extra cost` 100_000_000 `, paid earlier` 200_000_000 EQUALS 50_000_000

GIVEN claim IS A `A temporary accommodation claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under Part 3`
`the grounds against the owner's` claim MEANS
    `the grounds on which an accommodation claim fails, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` claim `, as at` `1 April 2026`

#ASSERT `the grounds against the owner's` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `occupier` `, months` 2 `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` 10_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the grounds against the owner's` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, unfit` FALSE `, as` `occupier` `, months` 2 `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` 10_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Accommodation: the Home is not unfit for occupation`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the owner's` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `another cause` `with` EMPTY) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `occupier` `, months` 2 `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` 10_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Accommodation: the damage was not caused by fire or another Insured Peril` `the cause is not one of the nine Insured Perils`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the owner's` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` (LIST `fermentation, natural heating or spontaneous combustion`)) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `occupier` `, months` 2 `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` 10_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Accommodation: the damage was not caused by fire or another Insured Peril` `Peril 1(a): fermentation, natural heating or spontaneous combustion`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the owner's` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` (LIST `war, invasion, foreign enemy, hostilities or civil war`)) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `occupier` `, months` 2 `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` 10_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `a General Exclusion` `General Exclusion 1(a): war, invasion, hostilities or civil war`)
-- F-p3-trigger: a Part 1 exclusion (wear and tear) is not a Part 3 ground; only the peril
-- test and the General Exclusions are.
#ASSERT `the grounds against the owner's` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` (LIST `wear and tear or depreciation`)) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `occupier` `, months` 2 `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` 10_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS EMPTY

-- Limb 1, rent: a landlord who lets the house and lives elsewhere (F-p3-rent). The premises
-- are not the Insured's residence, so they are neither the Insured Location nor a Home as
-- defined; limb 1 still applies on the reading taken. 2 months of 6: a third of 250,000,000.
GIVETH A `The insured premises`
`a house let to tenants` MEANS
    `The insured premises` WITH
        `the kind of building`                                     IS `a house`
        `at the address in the Policy Summary`                     IS TRUE
        `the Insured's principal personal residence`               IS FALSE
        `used wholly or mainly as the Insured's private residence` IS FALSE
        `part used as an office`                                   IS FALSE
        `office use approved by the authorities`                   IS FALSE
        `used for a trade or business other than an office`        IS FALSE
        `walls of concrete, brick or stone`                        IS TRUE
        `roof of concrete, tiles, slate or incombustible metal sheet` IS TRUE
        `under construction`                                       IS FALSE
        `being demolished or vacant pending demolition`            IS FALSE
        `a temporary building or structure`                        IS FALSE
        `enclosed by walls or fences`                              IS TRUE
        `some part is lent, let or sublet`                         IS TRUE
        `some part is used to manufacture, deposit or store goods` IS FALSE

GIVEN `rent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A temporary accommodation claim`
`the landlord's rent claim, rent lost` `rent` MEANS
    `an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `landlord not occupying the Insured Location`
        `, months` 2 `, rent lost` `rent` `, extra cost` 0 `, paid earlier` 0

#ASSERT `the grounds on which an accommodation claim fails, under` (`the owner's policy, at` `a house let to tenants`) `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the landlord's rent claim, rent lost` 60_000_000) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Part 3: the accommodation or rent payable, under` (`the owner's policy, at` `a house let to tenants`) `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the landlord's rent claim, rent lost` 60_000_000) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS 60_000_000
#ASSERT `Part 3: the accommodation or rent payable, under` (`the owner's policy, at` `a house let to tenants`) `with` `good conduct` `for` (`the landlord's rent claim, rent lost` 100_000_000) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS 250_000_000 DIVIDED BY 3
-- Limb 2 at the same let house: the occupier's limb needs a Home.
#ASSERT `the grounds on which an accommodation claim fails, under` (`the owner's policy, at` `a house let to tenants`) `with` `good conduct` `for` (`an accommodation claim: damage` (`the house damaged by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, unfit` TRUE `, as` `occupier` `, months` 2 `, rent lost` 0 `, extra cost` 10_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS (LIST `Accommodation, limb 2: the premises are not a Home`)

§§ `Part 3: the death benefit (src:656-666), forks F-death-amount, F-age, F-3-months`

GIVEN injured  IS A DATE
      died     IS A MAYBE DATE
      serious  IS A BOOLEAN
      inside   IS A BOOLEAN
      cause    IS A `A cause of injury`
GIVETH A `A death benefit claim`
`a death claim: injured on` injured `, died` died `, serious` serious `, inside` inside `, by` cause MEANS
    `A death benefit claim` WITH
        `the date of the injury`                        IS injured
        `the date of death`                             IS died
        `seriously injured`                             IS serious
        `in the Insured Location when injured`          IS inside
        `the cause of the injury`                       IS cause
        `the circumstances`                             IS EMPTY
        `paid under this benefit earlier in the Period` IS 0

GIVEN claim IS A `A death benefit claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under Part 3`
`the grounds against the death claim` claim MEANS
    `the grounds on which a death benefit claim fails, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` claim `, as at` `1 April 2026`

GIVETH A `A death benefit claim`
`a fire death on 1 May` MEANS
    `a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)) `, serious` TRUE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `fire`

#ASSERT `the grounds against the death claim` `a fire death on 1 May` EQUALS EMPTY
-- The limit is the lesser of 160,000,000 and 50% of 2,500,000,000: 160,000,000, paid in full.
#ASSERT `Part 3: the death benefit payable, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` `a fire death on 1 May` `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS 160_000_000
#ASSERT `the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) `, serious` TRUE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `theft`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 11)) `, serious` TRUE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `fire`) EQUALS (LIST `Death benefit: no death within 3 months of the injury`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, died` NOTHING `, serious` TRUE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `fire`) EQUALS (LIST `Death benefit: no death within 3 months of the injury`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)) `, serious` FALSE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `fire`) EQUALS (LIST `Death benefit: the Insured was not seriously injured`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)) `, serious` TRUE `, inside` FALSE `, by` `fire`) EQUALS (LIST `Death benefit: not injured while in the Insured Location`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)) `, serious` TRUE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `another cause`) EQUALS (LIST `Death benefit: the injury was not caused by fire or theft`)
-- Month-end: an injury on 30 November 2026 gives until 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT NOT elem `Death benefit: no death within 3 months of the injury` (`the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 11 30) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2027 2 28)) `, serious` TRUE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `fire`))
#ASSERT elem `Death benefit: no death within 3 months of the injury` (`the grounds against the death claim` (`a death claim: injured on` (YMD 2026 11 30) `, died` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1)) `, serious` TRUE `, inside` TRUE `, by` `fire`))

-- Age 5 to 65 in completed years on the day of the injury (10 March 2026).
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the owner's policy, the Insured born` born MEANS
    `a policy with` `the 2026 Summary` `, insured` (`The Insured person` WITH `date of birth` IS born, `owns the Home or is legally responsible for its care` IS TRUE, `a tenant of the Home` IS FALSE) `, premises` `a brick house`

GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the age bar applies, born` born MEANS
    elem `Death benefit: the Insured is not aged 5 to 65`
        (`the grounds on which a death benefit claim fails, under` (`the owner's policy, the Insured born` born) `with` `good conduct` `for` `a fire death on 1 May` `, as at` `1 April 2026`)

#ASSERT NOT `the age bar applies, born` (YMD 1960 3 11)
#ASSERT `the age bar applies, born` (YMD 1960 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT `the age bar applies, born` (YMD 2021 3 10)
#ASSERT `the age bar applies, born` (YMD 2021 3 11)
#ASSERT `age in completed years, born on` (YMD 1960 3 10) `, on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS 66
#ASSERT `age in completed years, born on` (YMD 1960 3 11) `, on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS 65
#ASSERT `age in completed years, born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `, on` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS 26

-- Not where the policy is issued to a company, or the Insured has Personal Accident cover.
GIVEN company IS A BOOLEAN
      pa      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the owner's policy, issued to a company` company `, with Personal Accident cover` pa MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `the Policy Summary`                                     IS `the 2026 Summary`
        `the Insured`                                            IS `an Insured born 15 June 1980, a tenant` FALSE
        `the premises`                                           IS `a brick house`
        `issued to a company`                                    IS company
        `the Insured also has Personal Accident cover`           IS pa
        `the Insurer agreed to issue a Certificate or the Policy Summary` IS TRUE
        `the Insurer received and accepted a completed Proposal Form`     IS TRUE
        `the premium was paid in full within the prescribed time`         IS TRUE
        `the premium paid`                                       IS 4_000_000

#ASSERT `the grounds on which a death benefit claim fails, under` (`the owner's policy, issued to a company` TRUE `, with Personal Accident cover` FALSE) `with` `good conduct` `for` `a fire death on 1 May` `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS (LIST `Death benefit: the policy is issued to a company`)
#ASSERT `the grounds on which a death benefit claim fails, under` (`the owner's policy, issued to a company` FALSE `, with Personal Accident cover` TRUE) `with` `good conduct` `for` `a fire death on 1 May` `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS (LIST `Death benefit: the Insured also has Personal Accident cover`)

-- The limit with a small Part 1: 200,000,000 insured in all gives 50%, 100,000,000.
#ASSERT `Part 3: the death benefit limit under` (`The Policy Summary` WITH `the Period of Insurance begins` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the Period of Insurance ends` IS YMD 2026 12 31, `the sum insured on the Home` IS NOTHING, `the sum insured on the Renovation Costs` IS NOTHING, `the sum insured on the Contents` IS JUST 200_000_000, `the Part 1 Limit of Liability` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for any one Occurrence` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for the Period` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 limit for food and drink` IS NOTHING, `the Part 1 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 3 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Insured is named under Part 3` IS TRUE, `the domestic helper benefit is named` IS FALSE, `the construction of the Home is specially provided for` IS FALSE, `the annual premium` IS 1_000_000) EQUALS 100_000_000
-- With nothing insured under Part 1, the lesser is nothing (F-total-si).
#ASSERT `Part 3: the death benefit limit under` (`The Policy Summary` WITH `the Period of Insurance begins` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the Period of Insurance ends` IS YMD 2026 12 31, `the sum insured on the Home` IS NOTHING, `the sum insured on the Renovation Costs` IS NOTHING, `the sum insured on the Contents` IS NOTHING, `the Part 1 Limit of Liability` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for any one Occurrence` IS JUST 1_000_000_000, `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for the Period` IS JUST 1_000_000_000, `the Part 2 limit for food and drink` IS NOTHING, `the Part 1 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 2 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Part 3 Deductible` IS NOTHING, `the Insured is named under Part 3` IS TRUE, `the domestic helper benefit is named` IS FALSE, `the construction of the Home is specially provided for` IS FALSE, `the annual premium` IS 1_000_000) EQUALS 0

§§ `Part 3: the domestic helper's personal effects (src:668-682)`

GIVEN loss      IS A `A Part 1 loss`
      requested IS A BOOLEAN
      observed  IS A BOOLEAN
      other     IS A BOOLEAN
      amount    IS A NUMBER
      `paid`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A domestic helper claim`
`a helper claim for` loss `, requested` requested `, observed` observed `, other insurance` other `, amount` amount `, paid earlier` `paid` MEANS
    `A domestic helper claim` WITH
        `requested by the Insured`                       IS requested
        `the loss`                                       IS loss
        `the helper observed the terms as if the Insured` IS observed
        `the helper is entitled under another insurance` IS other
        `the amount of the loss`                         IS amount
        `paid under this benefit earlier in the Period`  IS `paid`

GIVEN property IS A LIST OF `A description of property`
      owner    IS AN `An owner of property`
      place    IS A `A place where property was`
      cause    IS A `A cause of loss`
      cs       IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`the helper's` property `owned by` owner `at` place `, by` cause `with` cs MEANS
    `a loss to` `the Contents` `of` property `owned by` owner `at` place `on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `by` cause `with` cs `, unattended for` 0 `days`

GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`the helper's clothes burnt` MEANS
    `the helper's` (LIST `personal effects, normally carried or worn on the person`) `owned by` `a domestic helper` `at` `inside a lockable part of the Home` `, by` `fire` `with` EMPTY

GIVEN claim IS A `A domestic helper claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under Part 3`
`the grounds against the helper claim` claim MEANS
    `the grounds on which a domestic helper claim fails, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` claim `, as at` `1 April 2026`

GIVEN claim IS A `A domestic helper claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the helper is paid on` claim MEANS
    `Part 3: the domestic helper amount payable, under` `the owner's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` claim `, as at` `1 April 2026`

#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the helper is paid on` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS 3_000_000
#ASSERT `the helper is paid on` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 6_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS 4_000_000
#ASSERT `the helper is paid on` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 6_000_000 `, paid earlier` 3_000_000) EQUALS 1_000_000
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` FALSE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper: not requested by the Insured`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` TRUE `, observed` FALSE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper, proviso 1(a): the helper did not observe the terms`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` TRUE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper, proviso 1(b): the helper is entitled under another insurance`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` (`the helper's` (LIST `cash or coins`) `owned by` `a domestic helper` `at` `inside a lockable part of the Home` `, by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper: cash, banknotes, bank drafts or stamps`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` (`the helper's` (LIST `a bank draft or stamp`) `owned by` `a domestic helper` `at` `inside a lockable part of the Home` `, by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper: cash, banknotes, bank drafts or stamps`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` (`the helper's` (LIST `personal effects, normally carried or worn on the person`) `owned by` `the Insured` `at` `inside a lockable part of the Home` `, by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper: not the personal property of a domestic helper`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` (`the helper's` (LIST `personal effects, normally carried or worn on the person`) `owned by` `a domestic helper` `at` `away from the Insured Location` `, by` `fire` `with` EMPTY) `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper: the property was not kept at the Insured Location`)
#ASSERT `the grounds against the helper claim` (`a helper claim for` (`the helper's` (LIST `personal effects, normally carried or worn on the person`) `owned by` `a domestic helper` `at` `inside a lockable part of the Home` `, by` `theft or attempted theft` `with` EMPTY) `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) EQUALS (LIST `Helper: the loss was not caused by an Insured Peril` `Peril 9: no force or violence to enter or leave`)
-- The tenant's Summary does not name the benefit.
#ASSERT elem `Helper: the benefit is not named in the Policy Summary` (`the grounds on which a domestic helper claim fails, under` `the tenant's policy` `with` `good conduct` `for` (`a helper claim for` `the helper's clothes burnt` `, requested` TRUE `, observed` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, amount` 3_000_000 `, paid earlier` 0) `, as at` `1 April 2026`)

§§ `The General Conditions: grounds (src:800-915, 963-971)`

-- One test-only enumeration of the ways an Insured can depart from `good conduct`, so that
-- each test changes one fact and keeps the rest.
DECLARE `A departure` IS ONE OF
    `the terms not observed`
    `a Proposal Form statement untrue`
    `a misdescription`
    `the Insurer elected to avoid`
    `used other than as a residence`
    `the risk increased`
    `the property moved`
    `the interest passed`
    `the Insurer endorsed the change`
    `no immediate notice`
    `writs not forwarded`
    `liability admitted`
    `the police not notified`
    `no action to minimise`
    `other insurances not disclosed`
    `no proof of value`
    `no reasonable precautions`
    `the Insurer obstructed`
    `a fraudulent claim`
    `fraudulent means`
    `wilful or connivance`

GIVEN ds         IS A LIST OF `A departure`
      vacant     IS A NUMBER
      delivered  IS A MAYBE DATE
      extended   IS A MAYBE DATE
      rejected   IS A MAYBE DATE
      challenged IS A MAYBE DATE
      award      IS A MAYBE DATE
      `award challenged` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct`
`conduct with` ds `, vacant` vacant `, delivered` delivered `, extended to` extended `, rejected` rejected `, challenged` challenged `, award` award `, award challenged` `award challenged` MEANS
    `The Insured's conduct` WITH
        `observed and fulfilled the terms of the policy`                 IS NOT `d` `the terms not observed`
        `the statements in the Proposal Form were true`                  IS NOT `d` `a Proposal Form statement untrue`
        `misrepresented, misdescribed or omitted a matter in a document` IS `d` `a misdescription`
        `the Insurer elected to avoid the policy for misdescription`     IS `d` `the Insurer elected to avoid`
        `the Insured Location was used other than as a residence`        IS `d` `used other than as a residence`
        `precautions or circumstances changed so as to increase the risk` IS `d` `the risk increased`
        `the property was moved to another building or place`            IS `d` `the property moved`
        `consecutive days the Home had been vacant`                      IS vacant
        `the interest passed otherwise than by will or operation of law` IS `d` `the interest passed`
        `the Insurer endorsed its consent before the loss`               IS `d` `the Insurer endorsed the change`
        `gave immediate written notice with full particulars`            IS NOT `d` `no immediate notice`
        `forwarded every writ, summons and notice on receipt`            IS NOT `d` `writs not forwarded`
        `admitted or offered payment without written consent`            IS `d` `liability admitted`
        `notified the police immediately`                                IS NOT `d` `the police not notified`
        `acted immediately to minimise the loss`                         IS NOT `d` `no action to minimise`
        `disclosed all other insurances`                                 IS NOT `d` `other insurances not disclosed`
        `the date the written claim was delivered`                       IS delivered
        `the date to which the Insurer extended time in writing`         IS extended
        `kept receipts or proof of value`                                IS NOT `d` `no proof of value`
        `took reasonable precautions`                                    IS NOT `d` `no reasonable precautions`
        `obstructed or failed to comply with the Insurer's requirements` IS `d` `the Insurer obstructed`
        `the claim is fraudulent in any respect`                         IS `d` `a fraudulent claim`
        `used fraudulent means or devices`                               IS `d` `fraudulent means`
        `the loss was caused wilfully or with the Insured's connivance`  IS `d` `wilful or connivance`
        `the date the claim was rejected`                                IS rejected
        `the date the rejection was challenged`                          IS challenged
        `the date of an arbitral award on the claim`                     IS award
        `the date the award was challenged`                              IS `award challenged`
    WHERE
        `d` x MEANS elem x ds

-- The grounds for a fire on 10 March 2026 under Part 1, asked on 1 April 2026, the claim
-- delivered on 20 March, departing from good conduct as listed.
GIVEN ds IS A LIST OF `A departure`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under the General Conditions`
`the General Conditions grounds with` ds MEANS
    `the grounds under the General Conditions on` (`conduct with` ds `, vacant` 0 `, delivered` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, extended to` NOTHING `, rejected` NOTHING `, challenged` NOTHING `, award` NOTHING `, award challenged` NOTHING)
        `, event on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, theft` FALSE `, under` (LIST `Part 1`) `, as at` `1 April 2026`

#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `the terms not observed`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1: the terms of the policy were not observed`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `a Proposal Form statement untrue`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1: a statement in the Proposal Form was untrue`)
-- GC2: a misdescription alone is not enough; the Insurer must elect to avoid.
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `a misdescription`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `a misdescription`, `the Insurer elected to avoid`) EQUALS (LIST `GC2: the Insurer avoided the policy for misdescription`)
-- GC3: each change, unless the Insurer endorsed it before the loss.
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `used other than as a residence`) EQUALS (LIST `GC3(a): the Insured Location used other than as a residence`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `the risk increased`) EQUALS (LIST `GC3(b): precautions or circumstances changed so as to increase the risk`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `the property moved`) EQUALS (LIST `GC3(c): the property moved to another building or place`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `the interest passed`) EQUALS (LIST `GC3(e): the interest passed otherwise than by will or operation of law`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `used other than as a residence`, `the risk increased`, `the property moved`, `the interest passed`, `the Insurer endorsed the change`) EQUALS EMPTY
-- GC4 through GC1, GC12, proof of value, GC5, GC7(a).
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `no immediate notice`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with GC4(a): no immediate written notice with full particulars`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `writs not forwarded`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with GC4(b): a writ, summons or notice not forwarded on receipt`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `liability admitted`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with GC4(c): liability admitted or payment offered without written consent`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `no action to minimise`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with GC4(e): no immediate action to minimise the loss`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `other insurances not disclosed`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with GC4(f): other insurances not disclosed`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `no proof of value`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with Part 1: no receipts or proof of value kept`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `no reasonable precautions`) EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with GC12: reasonable precautions not taken`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `the Insurer obstructed`) EQUALS (LIST `GC5: the Insured obstructed the Insurer or did not comply with its requirements`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `a fraudulent claim`) EQUALS (LIST `GC7(a): the claim is fraudulent`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `fraudulent means`) EQUALS (LIST `GC7(a): fraudulent means or devices were used`)
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `wilful or connivance`) EQUALS (LIST `GC7(a): the loss was caused wilfully or with the Insured's connivance`)
-- GC4(d) only for theft or malicious persons: police not notified of a fire is no ground.
#ASSERT `the General Conditions grounds with` (LIST `the police not notified`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the grounds under the General Conditions on` (`conduct with` (LIST `the police not notified`) `, vacant` 0 `, delivered` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, extended to` NOTHING `, rejected` NOTHING `, challenged` NOTHING `, award` NOTHING `, award challenged` NOTHING) `, event on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, theft` TRUE `, under` (LIST `Part 1`) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS (LIST `GC1 with GC4(d): the police not notified of a theft or malicious act`)
-- Proof of value is a Part 1 duty: a Part 2 claim is not defeated by it.
#ASSERT `the grounds under the General Conditions on` (`conduct with` (LIST `no proof of value`) `, vacant` 0 `, delivered` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, extended to` NOTHING `, rejected` NOTHING `, challenged` NOTHING `, award` NOTHING `, award challenged` NOTHING) `, event on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, theft` FALSE `, under` (LIST `Part 2`) `, as at` `1 April 2026` EQUALS EMPTY

