§§ `Traces of the duties (Layer 3). Each trace starts AT 0 on the day of the event; days are calendar days.`

-- GC4: notice on day 1, written claim on day 30 (in time), the Insurer pays on day 45.
#TRACE `GC4: the Insured's notice and claim, with days allowed` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give written notice of the event with full particulars` AT 1
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `deliver a written claim with particulars and evidence` AT 30
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `pay the claim` AT 45
-- The written claim on day 31: breach of GC4(g) by the Insured.
#TRACE `GC4: the Insured's notice and claim, with days allowed` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give written notice of the event with full particulars` AT 1
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `deliver a written claim with particulars and evidence` AT 31
-- The claim in on day 10 and nothing paid by day 400: the Insurer's duty stands, with no
-- deadline in the document (Law art 31 would supply 15 days; not encoded).
#TRACE `GC4: the Insured's notice and claim, with days allowed` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give written notice of the event with full particulars` AT 1
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `deliver a written claim with particulars and evidence` AT 10
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- GC4(c): an admission without consent breaches the prohibition.
#TRACE `GC4(c): no admission or offer without written consent` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `admit, negotiate, offer, promise or pay without written consent` AT 5
-- GC5: obstruction breaches; the Insurer's power alone, used, fulfils its side.
#TRACE `GC5: the Insurer may take possession; the Insured shall not obstruct or abandon` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `enter and take possession of the premises or property` AT 2
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `obstruct the Insurer in exercising its powers` AT 3
-- GC11: the Insurer cancels and refunds.
#TRACE `GC11: the Insurer may cancel, and must then refund` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `send written notice of cancellation by registered post` AT 0
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `refund premium` AT 40
-- GC10: either party may go to VIAC; the Insured does.
#TRACE `GC10: either party may refer a dispute to VIAC` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `submit the dispute to VIAC` AT 10
